    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0848" n="1806" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1806"/>

                <head>No. 39.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 25, 1888</date>.
                        (Received May 26.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 30th of April I had the honor to
                    address you, as instructed by the Marquis of Salisbury, on the subject of the
                    appeals pending in the cases of British vessels seized by the United States in
                    Behring’s Sea, and Her Majesty’s Government have now requested me to ask you for
                    a reply to my above-mentioned communication.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
